WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.450
In a letter to Christians in Rome, the
apostle Paul noticed something striking.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.390
People who did not have the Jewish law
still did much of what it required.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:16.190
Centuries later, Richard Dawkins argued
that our moral sense has Darwinian roots.

4
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.870
And James Rachels asked whether worship
itself clashes with being a free moral

5
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.090
agent.

6
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.880
So do people need God to be good,
or can religion get in the way?

7
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.140
In this mission, you'll pull apart the
different ways morality might depend on

8
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:31.930
God.

9
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.830
Then you'll test the critics and the
believers' replies on an argument map.

10
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.910
Your mission: weigh up whether
being good depends on God.
